You are executing the saas-trust-center-document-pack skill. Mandate: produce Trust_Center_Document_Pack.md and per-section public-facing markdown.

1. Read Compliance_Docs.md, Data_Isolation_Evidence_Pack.md, Risk_Assessment.md, DPA, sub-processor list.
2. Produce the Security Overview page: encryption at rest, encryption in transit, auth (SSO, MFA), authz, tenant isolation, vuln mgmt, secure SDLC, pentest cadence, incident response, data residency.
3. Produce the Compliance Attestations index table. Status options: held, in progress, planned, not applicable. Include report-request form URL placeholder.
4. Produce the Sub-Processor List: name, purpose, region, data classes processed, certifications. Include the 30-day advance-notice commitment.
5. Produce the DPA & privacy section linking the published DPA, privacy policy, cookie policy, data-residency options, breach-notification commitment (72 h GDPR / 72 h ISO / per-jurisdiction).
6. Produce the Vulnerability Disclosure Policy: reporting channel, safe-harbour scope, response SLA, hall-of-fame / bounty.
7. Produce the Status Page commitment: public URL, incident-comms protocol, postmortem-publication commitment.
8. Produce the Customer Data Handling summary: data classes, retention defaults, deletion options, export options, residency, encryption posture per class.
9. Write Trust_Center_Document_Pack.md as the master index. Place each section's public markdown under public/trust/.

Validation: Halt if any attestation row claims "held" without an auditor name and period. Halt if sub-processor list is empty. Halt if vulnerability disclosure policy lacks a reporting channel or response SLA.
